{"name":"Vegan Villain","hex":"#aa9911","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"vegan","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a product or practice, especially food, not containing animal products (meat, eggs, milk, leather, etc.) or inherently involving animal use.","Of a person, committed to avoiding any product or practice that inherently involves animal use."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who does not eat, drink or otherwise consume any animal products","A person committed to avoiding products and practices that inherently involve animal use, including all foods containing animal products, and to abstaining from direct and intentional harm to animals as far as possible; an adherent to veganism."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vegan"},{"term":"villain","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["(Can we clean up this sense?) A vile, wicked person.\n\nAn extremely depraved person, or one capable or guilty of great crimes.\nA deliberate scoundrel.","An extremely depraved person, or one capable or guilty of great crimes."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To debase; to degrade .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/villain"}],"entries":[{"title":"Veganism","blocks":[{"text":"Veganism is the practice of abstaining from the use of animal products and the consumption of animal source foods, and an associated philosophy that rejects the commodity status of animals. A person who practices veganism is known as a vegan; the word is also used to describe foods and materials that are compatible with veganism."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Vegan_friendly_icon.svg/330px-Vegan_friendly_icon.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Veganism"},{"title":"Villain","blocks":[{"text":"A villain is a real person or fictional character who is defined as a cruel and malicious person involved in or devoted to wickedness or crime; or a character in a play, novel, or the like, who constitutes an important evil agency in the plot\". The antonym of a villain is a hero."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Bela_Lugosi_as_Dracula.jpg/330px-Bela_Lugosi_as_Dracula.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Villain"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Gandhi_LVS_1931.jpg/500px-Gandhi_LVS_1931.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Gandhi_LVS_1931.jpg/500px-Gandhi_LVS_1931.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mahatma Gandhi, London Vegetarian Society, 20 November 1931, with Henry S. Salt on his right[f]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGandhi_LVS_1931.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Barbara_Moore_%281961%29.jpg/500px-Barbara_Moore_%281961%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Barbara_Moore_%281961%29.jpg/1280px-Barbara_Moore_%281961%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Barbara_Moore_%281961%29.jpg/500px-Barbara_Moore_%281961%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Barbara Moore attended the first meeting of The Vegan Society as an observer.[58]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABarbara_Moore_(1961).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Patrik_Baboumian_f%C3%BCr_PETA.jpg/500px-Patrik_Baboumian_f%C3%BCr_PETA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"htt